{"agent":"buglane23","data":{"auto":false,"dedupe":{"answer":"extends","candidates":[{"id":"B-budget-stop-fragment-impact","score":0.718375794},{"id":"fix-B-budget-stop-fragment-impact","score":0.686437526}],"score":0.718375794,"target":"B-budget-stop-fragment-impact"},"relation":"extends","score":0.718375794,"text":"Why does the upgrade manifest fail to load on main, and what single change fixes it?\nUM.load() raises ManifestError on main because the unreleased fragment knob_added.swarm.budget_stop_enabled.toml declares impact='behavior', not one of IMPACTS=(additive, deprecating, breaking).\nupgrade_manifest._change() raises ManifestError when impact is non-empty and not in IMPACTS; load() parses every unreleased/ fragment, so the invalid impact breaks the whole manifest and every consumer (lint, upgrade apply, version lint).","who":"buglane23"},"id":"e01ea1f7ed3a256d8b66b17b7","kind":"record.extended","lamport":196843,"schema":1,"subject":"B-budget-stop-fragment-impact","ts":"2026-11-13T21:34:07.071415Z"}
